DIDSSO runtime setup
====================

All active components are located below this DIDSSO directory.

Create or update both Python runtimes once:

    .\setup-runtime.ps1

The script creates .venv-didcomm for IdP/RP and the independent environment
firefox-extension\.venv for the extension backend. IdP and RP never import
dependencies from the extension environment. Set DIDSSO_PYTHON only to
override the shared IdP/RP backend interpreter.

Reset state
-----------

Persistent native runtime data is stored in IdP\data, RP\data, and
firefox-extension\data. DIDSSO_DATA_DIR overrides the data directory for one
component; do not point different participants at the same directory. The IdP
web server and its protocol backend must use the same IdP data directory.
Reset also removes the RISC Zero and STWO registration signing keys and the RP
scope configuration. Keys are regenerated on demand, and the RP uses its
profile/email scope defaults. Docker volumes and Firefox extension storage are
not reset by the local procedure. Stop all services before resetting and
restart them afterwards.

Preview and validate all reset targets without changing data:

    .\reset-state.ps1 -ValidateOnly
    .\reset-state.ps1 -WhatIf

Perform the reset explicitly:

    .\reset-state.ps1

Registration proof backends
---------------------------

The default backend is RISC Zero. To use STWO in a PowerShell terminal, set:

    $env:DIDSSO_PROOF_BACKEND = "stwo"

Start IdP and RP with the same backend. Switching the backend requires a
registration credential issued for that backend.

An RP needs a seperate registration with the IdP for each proof backend.

The STWO upstream source is not vendored into this repository. Install or
update its pinned WSL/Linux source and binaries once from the DIDSSO root:

    wsl bash ./zk-stark/setup_stwo.sh

The setup checks out the commit recorded in zk-stark/STWO_COMMIT and applies
the versioned compatibility patch from zk-stark/patches.

Start the services
------------------

1. Run `cargo run` in RP (port 3002 is configured by Cargo).
2. Run `.\start.ps1` in RP\didcomm-backend.
3. Run `cargo run` in IdP (port 3001 is configured by Cargo).
4. Run `.\start.ps1` in IdP\didcomm-backend.
5. Run .\start.ps1 in firefox-extension\backend.
6. Load firefox-extension\manifest.json as a temporary Firefox add-on at
   about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox.

The RP uses https://127.0.0.1:3001 as the browser-facing IdP origin. To
override it, set this variable before starting the RP backend:

    $env:DIDSSO_IDP_WEB_PUBLIC_URL = "https://127.0.0.1:3001"

Use the Master DID from that IdP's homepage to register the RP in the RP
admin dashboard, then accept the registration at the IdP. The RP stores the
Master DID with the configured web origin after acceptance. After a full
reset, repeat registration without changing the startup configuration.

The DIDComm start scripts configure the selected proof backend and the larger
Authlib JWE ciphertext limit. RISC Zero and STWO continue to use their WSL
wrappers from zk-risc0 and zk-stark on Windows.
